QUESTION 11: LIBRARY BOOK ISSUE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
============================================================

A college library wants to develop a simple book issue management system. For every book, the system should store a unique book ID, title, author name, price, and an availability status indicating whether the book is currently available for issue. The availability information should be maintained internally by the program and should not be modified directly from outside the class.

The program should maintain information for multiple books using an array of objects. Suitable constructors should be provided to initialize book information. The program should provide functions to accept book details, display complete book information, issue a book, return a book, and obtain the book ID for searching purposes.

When a user requests a book, the program should ask for the book ID and search the collection. If the requested book is available, it should be issued and its availability status should be changed. If the book is already issued, the program should display an appropriate message. Similarly, when a book is returned, its availability status should be restored.

The main program should be menu driven and repeatedly display options such as:
1. Enter book details
2. Display all books
3. Issue a book
4. Return a book
5. Exit

The program should continue executing until the user selects the exit option.


