QUESTION 14: ONLINE SHOPPING CART
============================================================

An online shopping application wants to maintain a customer's shopping cart. Each product added to the cart should contain a product ID, product name, unit price, and quantity purchased. The application should be able to manage several products using an array of product objects.

The program should provide functions to accept and display product information. It should also provide a function to calculate the total cost of a particular product by multiplying its unit price by its quantity.

A separate function outside the class should receive a product object by reference and update the quantity of the original product. Another function should receive a product object as a constant reference and display the product details without allowing any modification to the object.

The program should allow the user to change the quantity of a selected product and should recalculate the total shopping cart bill after the change. The total cart bill should be obtained by adding the individual totals of all products.

The main program should provide a menu containing operations such as:
1. Enter product details
2. Display all products
3. Update the quantity of a product
4. Calculate and display the total shopping cart bill
5. Exit

The program should continue to display the menu until the user chooses to exit.


