QUESTION 15: HOSPITAL PATIENT BILLING SYSTEM
============================================================

A hospital wants to maintain information about admitted patients and calculate their final hospital bills. Basic patient information such as patient ID, patient name, and age is common to all patients. An admitted patient additionally has room charge per day, number of days admitted, doctor consultation charges, and medicine charges.

Design the program using inheritance. Store the common patient information in a base class and the hospitalization and billing information in a derived class.

The program should provide functions to accept and display patient information. The derived class should calculate the hospital bill using the following components:

Total Bill =
(Room Charge Per Day × Number of Days Admitted)
+ Doctor Consultation Charges
+ Medicine Charges

The program should maintain information for multiple admitted patients using an array of objects. It should display the details and calculated bill of each patient. It should also compare the bills and identify the patient having the highest total hospital bill.

The main program should be menu driven with options such as:
1. Enter patient details
2. Display all patient details
3. Calculate and display hospital bills
4. Find and display the patient having the highest bill
5. Exit

The menu should continue until the user selects the exit option.